e search going?\"\n\n15 00:00:56.890 – 00:00:59.720 => \"Okay. Everything is really expensive.\"\n\n16 00:01:00.920 – 00:01:03.750 => \"I know exactly what you mean.\"\n\n17 00:01:04.450 – 00:01:07.610 => \"I have a viewing at eleven today.\"\n\n18 00:01:08.560 – 00:01:11.335 => \"Do you want me to come with you?\"\n\n19 00:01:12.535 – 00:01:15.475 => \"No need, but thanks.\"\n\n20 00:01:16.175 – 00:01:19.500 => \"Hey, it's going to rain. Do you have an umbrella?\"\n\n21 00:01:20.450 – 00:01:23.225 => \"No, I left it at home.\"\n\n22 00:01:24.425 – 00:01:26.980 => \"Here, take mine.\"\n\n23 00:01:27.680 – 00:01:29.850 => \"Are you sure?\"\n\n24 00:01:30.800 – 00:01:34.345 => \"Absolutely. Give it back to me tonight.\"\n\n25 00:01:35.545 – 00:01:37.935 => \"Okay, I owe you one.\"\n\n26 00:01:38.635 – 00:01:42.510 => \"Don't worry. Shall we have dinner at nine?\"\n\n27 00:01:43.460 – 00:01:45.795 => \"Sounds great.\"\n\n28 00:01:47.000 – 00:01:49.660 => \"Perfect.\"\n\n29 00:01:50.360 – 00:01:52.860 => \"Here's your coffee.\"\n\n30 00:01:53.810 – 00:01:57.410 => \"Thank you very much. Have a nice day!\"\n\n... then skip to:\n\n31 00:02:05.610 – 00:02:08.440 => \"Excuse me, could you help me?\"\n\n32 00:02:09.140 – 00:02:11.310 => \"Of course, go ahead.\"\n\n33 00:02:12.260 – 00:02:15.255 => \"I'm looking for the train to the city centre.\"\n\n34 00:02:16.460 – 00:02:19.060 => \"It leaves from platform four.\"\n\n35 00:02:19.760 – 00:02:22.710 => \"What time does the next one leave?\"\n\n36 00:02:23.660 – 00:02:27.530 => \"At quarter past ten, but it's running late today.\"\n\n37 00:02:28.730 – 00:02:31.720 => \"Late? How long?\"\n\n38 00:02:32.430 – 00:02:35.640 => \"About twenty minutes, more or less.\"\n\n39 00:02:36.590 – 00:02:39.750 => \"Oh no. I have an appointment at eleven.\"\n\n40 00:02:40.950 – 00:02:44.440 => \"Then you'd better take the bus.\"\n\n41 00:02:45.140 – 00:02:48.190 => \"Is the stop far from here?\"\n\n42 00:02:49.140 – 00:02:52.355 => \"No, it'